</div>           <div class="content">
            <div class="main-content-wrapper"><div class="main" role="main">
                                      <div class="content-outer-border"><div class="content-inner-border">
                                                                                <a id="main-content"></a>
                    <div class="title-wrapper"><h1 id="page-title">City Elections</h1></div>                      <div class="region region-content">
    <div id="block-system-main" class="block block-system">
    <div class='block-header'>
                            </div>
    <div class="block-content">
    	
<div id="node-8901" class="node node-page clearfix" about="/clerk/page/city-elections-0" typeof="sioc:Item foaf:Document">

      <span property="dc:title" content="City Elections" class="rdf-meta element-hidden"></span>
  


<div class="content_main">
<div class="field field-name-body field-type-text-with-summary field-label-hidden"><div class="field-items"><div class="field-item even" property="content:encoded"><h4>Local Ballot Measures</h4>
<p><span><span><strong><span><span>Election Day is Tuesday, November 3, 2026.</span></span></strong></span></span></p>
<p>Register to Vote: You may register at any time, but to be eligible to vote in an upcoming election, your Voter Registration Form must be submitted online by midnight no later than Monday, October 19th, 2026. If you are mailing a Voter Registration Form, it must be postmarked no later than Monday, October 19th, 2026.</p>
<p><span><span><span>East Palo Alto voters will consider two local ballot measures and elect <strong><span><span>two City Councilmembers</span></span></strong> during the November 3, 2026, General Municipal Election.</span></span></span></p>
<p><strong>East Palo Alto Community/Water/Public Safety Infrastructure Measure O:</strong> </p>
<p class="MsoNoSpacing"><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>Measure O is the East Palo Alto Community, Water and Public Safety Infrastructure Measure.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>If approved by voters, Measure O funding would address community-identified priorities such as providing safe and clean drinking water, replacing deteriorating pipes that distribute drinking water, expanding safe places for children and teens, repairing aging storm drains to prevent flooding on City streets, and establishing an up-to-date Emergency Command Center while addressing earthquake safety needs at public facilities.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p class="isselectedend"><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>More than 40 years old, the East Palo Alto Library is outdated, deteriorating, and overcrowded, with wait lists for literacy and children's programming due to a lack of space.  A modern library with up-to-date technology, hands-on learning, and dedicated areas for children and teens so they have somewhere safe to go after school and during the summer is envisioned as an outcome of Measure O.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p class="isselectedend"><img alt="" src="data:image/png;base64," style="height:271px; width:578px" /></p>
<p class="isselectedend"> </p>
<p><a href="https://www.cityofepa.org/sites/default/files/fileattachments/city_clerk/page/8901/measure_o_-_resolution_and_full_text.pdf">Resolution and Full Text</a><br />
<a href="https://www.cityofepa.org/sites/default/files/fileattachments/city_clerk/page/8901/measure_o_-_impartial_analysis.pdf">Impartial Analysis</a><br />
<a href="https://www.cityofepa.org/sites/default/files/fileattachments/city_clerk/page/8901/measure_o_-_argument_in_favor.pdf">Primary Argument in Favor</a><br />
<a href="https://www.cityofepa.org/sites/default/files/fileattachments/city_clerk/page/8901/measure_o_-_rebuttal_to_argument_against.pdf">Rebuttal to Argument Against</a><br />
<a href="https://www.cityofepa.org/sites/default/files/fileattachments/city_clerk/page/8901/measure_o_-_argument_against.pdf">Primary Argument Against</a></p>
<p><strong>East Palo Alto Term Limits Measure CC</strong></p>
<p>Measure CC is the East Palo Alto City Council Term Limits Measure. Measure CC allows voters to decide whether to establish City Council term limits. If approved, no person would be eligible to serve more than three consecutive full terms on the East Palo Alto City Council. A partial term of more than two years would count as one full term.</p>
<table cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse; width:572px">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td rowspan="2" style="border-bottom:2px double black; border-left:2px double black; border-right:2px double black; border-top:2px double black; height:83px; vertical-align:top; width:501px">
<p>Shall the measure providing that no person shall be eligible to serve for more than three (3) consecutive full terms on the City Council be adopted, with service of partial terms exceeding two years qualifying as a full term?</p>
</td>
<td style="border-bottom:2px double black; border-left:none; border-right:2px double black; border-top:2px double black; height:83px; width:71px">
<p>YES</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="border-bottom:2px double black; border-left:none; border-right:2px double black; border-top:none; height:83px; width:71px">
<p class="MsoHeading9"><em>NO</em></p>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p> </p>
<p><a href="https://www.cityofepa.org/sites/default/files/fileattachments/city_clerk/page/8901/measure_cc_-_resolution_and_full_text_2.pdf">Resolution and Full Text</a><br />
<a href="https://www.cityofepa.org/sites/default/files/fileattachments/city_clerk/page/8901/measure_cc_-_impartial_analysis.pdf">Impartial Analysis</a><br />
<a href="https://www.cityofepa.org/sites/default/files/fileattachments/city_clerk/page/8901/measure_cc_-_arguments_in_favor.pdf">Primary Argument in Favor</a><br />
<a href="https://www.cityofepa.org/sites/default/files/fileattachments/city_clerk/page/8901/measure_cc_-_rebuttal_to_argument_in_favor.pdf">Rebuttal to Argument in Favor</a><br />
<a href="https://www.cityofepa.org/sites/default/files/fileattachments/city_clerk/page/8901/measure_cc_-_arguments_against.pdf">Primary Argument Against</a></p>
<p><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><strong>Make sure your vote is counted!</strong></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p class="MsoBodyText"><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>Due to recent USPS operational changes, ballots mailed too late may not arrive in time to be counted. If you plan to vote by mail, please return your ballot as early as possible and ideally to an official Vote by Mail Drop Box. Please remember to register to vote by Monday, October 19th, 2026.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p class="MsoBodyText"><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span><em>*This is for informational purposes only.  The City of East Palo Alto does not advocate for or against any measure.</em></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>November 3, 2026 Election</h4>
<h2>CANDIDATES RUNNING FOR 2026 CITY COUNCIL</h2>
<p>The City of East Palo Alto will conduct local elections with the State elections on November 3, 2026. The City will hold an election for two(2) Council Members to four (4) year terms beginning in December 2026. </p>
<p>The complete San Mateo County November 3, 2026 certified results will be available at the County Elections page within the Statement of the Vote. For full San Mateo County election results, visit: <a href="https://smcacre.gov/elections/november-3-2026-statewide-general-election">San Mateo County Elections Results Page</a>.</p>
<p>To schedule an appointment to receive your candidate documents, email the City Clerk's office at: <a href="&#109;&#97;&#105;&#108;&#116;&#111;&#58;&#99;&#105;&#116;&#121;&#99;&#108;&#101;&#114;&#107;&#64;&#99;&#105;&#116;&#121;&#111;&#102;&#101;&#112;&#97;&#46;&#111;&#114;&#103;">&#99;&#105;&#116;&#121;&#99;&#108;&#101;&#114;&#107;&#64;&#99;&#105;&#116;&#121;&#111;&#102;&#101;&#112;&#97;&#46;&#111;&#114;&#103;</a>. The City Clerk will be available Monday-Friday from 8:00 am - 5:00 PM</p>
<h2><u><strong>The Secretary of State recommends voters do not vote by regular mail anymore, as their ballots may not be registered in time. Please vote at one of the three following voting centers or drop off your ballots at any one of the following locations.</strong></u></h2>
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width:95%">
<caption>
